{
	title: 'SAVE_SECRET tool prompts user and writes env secrets on the host',
	spec: 'Agent tool SAVE_SECRET /* <purpose> */ { file, name } prompts the user with a hidden secret form (skip: true) and writes NAME=value atomically (temp file + rename, mode 0600, tightening existing files) to the env file on the host. The secret value travels only from client to host and never enters history, events, logs, or tool results; the agent receives only saved, canceled (Escape or empty input), or an error. Replaces an existing NAME= line or appends NAME=value without losing other lines, creating the file if missing. Warns in the question text ("This replaces the current value.") when the variable already exists. Validates name as [A-Z_][A-Z0-9_]*, refuses values containing CR/LF or NUL, and refuses files inside a git work tree unless git-ignored (git check-ignore) as well as paths inside .git. Tool card titles use the /* purpose */ comment or fall back to "Save <NAME> to <file>". System prompt Other tools lists the one-line call example and description; HELP SAVE_SECRET documents full usage.',
